{
  "generated_description": "The catalog provides Census 2001 data on migrants, covering place of last residence, age, sex, marital status, and duration of residence for the 0–9 years range. It supports analysis of migrant characteristics such as never married, currently married, widowed, and divorced/separated categories, along with residence-based breakdowns. Published by the Ministry of Home Affairs and the Registrar General and Census Commissioner, India, the collection is intended for demographic research, planning, and policy work on migration patterns across India and its states.",
  "generated_sector": "Census and Surveys; Census"
}

{
  "generated_description": "The catalog brings together Census 2001 statistics on migrants, covering place of last residence, age, sex, reason for migration, and duration of residence. It supports analysis of migration patterns for work/employment, business, education, marriage, and household-related movement, including migrants moved after birth. Published by the Ministry of Home Affairs and the Registrar General and Census Commissioner, India, the resources enable demographic and socio-economic studies of migration across India and its states for the 2001 census.",
  "generated_sector": "Census and Surveys; Census"
}

{
  "generated_description": "The catalog brings together Census 2001 data on migrants, focusing on place of last residence, duration of residence, and reason for migration. It supports analysis of migrant characteristics by sex and residence, including migrants from within India and from outside India, with breakdowns covering countries in Asia and other countries. Published by the Ministry of Home Affairs and the Registrar General and Census Commissioner, India, the collection is useful for migration studies and policy planning using Census 2001 evidence for India.",
  "generated_sector": "Census and Surveys; Census"
}

{
  "generated_description": "The catalog brings together Census 2001 statistics on migrants by place of last residence, economic activity, age, sex, and duration of residence. It covers categories such as main workers, marginal workers, non-workers, and those seeking or available for work, along with migrant distributions by residence and demographic attributes. Published by the Ministry of Home Affairs and the Registrar General and Census Commissioner, India, the collection supports research and planning on migration patterns across India and its States for Census 2001.",
  "generated_sector": "Census and Surveys; Census"
}

{
  "generated_description": "The catalog focuses on milk procurement and milk consumption for the City of Kota, Rajasthan. It supports analysis of how much milk is procured and how it is consumed within the city, helping urban planners and program managers assess local dairy supply and demand. The work is aligned with the Ministry of Housing and Urban Affairs under the Smart Cities Mission, with a focus on city-level insights for Kota.",
  "generated_sector": "Food; Consumer Affairs"
}

{
  "generated_description": "The catalog covers mill production of cotton cloth in India, tracking output measured in million square metres. It spans 2000-01 to 2011-12, supporting analysis of trends in the textile manufacturing sector. The series is useful for researchers, planners, and industry stakeholders who need consistent time-series indicators for monitoring production performance and demand-supply dynamics. Published by the Ministry of Statistics and Programme Implementation.",
  "generated_sector": "Industries; Statistics"
}

{
  "generated_description": "The catalog covers mill production of cotton yarn in India, providing time-series estimates in Mn. Kg. for All India from 2000-01 to 2011-12. It also includes state-wise details for 2010-11 and 2011-12, supporting comparisons across regions and periods. These statistics are useful for monitoring textile industry output, assessing production trends, and informing planning and policy analysis. The data are published by the Ministry of Statistics and Programme Implementation.",
  "generated_sector": "Industries; Statistics"
}

{
  "generated_description": "The catalog brings together information on min, max, and average water levels for Ujjain. It supports monitoring and comparison of water level variations over time for urban water management and planning under the Smart Cities Mission. The focus is on the City of Ujjain, Madhya Pradesh, enabling stakeholders to assess trends relevant to groundwater or water resource status and to inform local interventions. Published under the Ministry of Housing and Urban Affairs, with involvement from Madhya Pradesh and Ujjain.",
  "generated_sector": "Environment and Forest; Water Quality"
}

{
  "generated_description": "The catalog brings together mineral and state wise resources reserves data for India, supporting analysis of availability and distribution of key mineral resources. It is useful for planning, policy formulation, and research by enabling comparisons across states and minerals. Published by the Ministry of Mines through the Indian Bureau of Mines, the resources help track reserves information relevant to mining and related decision-making.",
  "generated_sector": "Industries; Mining"
}

{
  "generated_description": "Mineral-wise Summary Of Mining Lease Distribution compiles information on mining lease distribution across India, organized by mineral. It supports analysis of how mining rights are allocated and where mining activity is concentrated by mineral type. Published by the Ministry of Mines and the Indian Bureau of Mines, the catalog is useful for policy planning, regulatory monitoring, and research on the mining sector’s spatial and mineral-wise distribution.",
  "generated_sector": "Industries; Mining"
}

{
  "generated_description": "Covers Minimum Support Price/Procurement Price for Crops on a crop year basis across India, providing commodity-wise MSP/procurement rates (typically per quintal) for major crops such as paddy, rice, cotton, and sugarcane. The series supports analysis of government procurement pricing and its role in safeguarding farmers’ interests. Published by the Ministry of Finance, Department of Economic Affairs, the data is useful for policy review, market and price trend studies, and planning for agricultural stakeholders.",
  "generated_sector": "Finance; Economy"
}

{
  "generated_description": "The catalog provides Ministry/Department-wise outlay estimates for transport sectors under the Twelfth Five Year Plan (2012-17) for India. It covers Gross Budgetary Support (GBS) outlay as well as Internal and Extra Budgetary Resources (IEBR), supporting analysis of planned funding flows across transport ministries and departments. The data is useful for policy review, budget tracking, and comparative assessment of resource composition for transport sector planning. It is published by NITI Aayog.",
  "generated_sector": "Transport; Road Transport"
}

{
  "generated_description": "The catalog brings together Ministry/Department-wise outlay information for the Industry sector under the 12th Five-Year Plan (2012-17). It covers budgetary support and internal and extra budgetary resources (IEBR) allocated to different Ministries/Departments for industry-related planning and implementation. The data supports policy analysis, monitoring of plan financing, and comparisons of sectoral resource allocation across government departments. Published by NITI Aayog for India-wide planning.",
  "generated_sector": "Industries; Manufacturing"
}

{
  "generated_description": "Mission Antyodaya Survey Data supports a convergence and accountability framework for rural development, focusing on how resources allocated by multiple Government of India ministries and departments are used through programme implementation. The annual survey is conducted in Gram Panchayats across India to inform planning and monitoring, including Gram Panchayat Development Plan processes under Mission Antyodaya and related initiatives. Published by the Ministry of Rural Development / Department of Rural Development (DRD), the data is useful for assessing rural service delivery and strengthening local-level governance.",
  "generated_sector": "Rural; Development"
}

{
  "generated_description": "The catalog focuses on mobility (traffic) in Agra, Uttar Pradesh, covering actions taken using ITMS to identify vehicles violating rules and contributing to pollution. It supports understanding traffic-related compliance and pollution drivers in the city, enabling monitoring and targeted interventions for cleaner, safer urban mobility. Published under the Smart Cities Mission by the Ministry of Housing and Urban Affairs, with involvement from Uttar Pradesh and Agra.",
  "generated_sector": "Transport; Road Transport"
}

{
  "generated_description": "The catalog focuses on mobility infrastructure in Kohima, Nagaland, supporting planning and improvement of urban transport services. It covers transport-related assets and indicators relevant to local connectivity, including bus and transportation infrastructure. Published under the Ministry of Housing and Urban Affairs through the Smart Cities Mission, the resources are intended to help stakeholders assess current mobility conditions and guide upgrades for smoother movement within the city.",
  "generated_sector": "Transport; Road Transport"
}

{
  "generated_description": "The catalog brings together information on modes of transport in Bhubaneswar, covering options such as walking, cycling, auto-rickshaws, buses, shared services, and rail/metro connectivity where available. It is intended to support urban mobility planning and service improvement by helping users understand how people move within the city. Published under the Ministry of Housing and Urban Affairs through the Smart Cities Mission, with a focus on Bhubaneswar, Odisha.",
  "generated_sector": "Transport; Road Transport"
}

{
  "generated_description": "The catalog provides mode-wise and sector-wise break-ups of power generation in Billion Units for India. It supports analysis of how electricity generation is distributed across different modes and sectors, enabling comparisons for planning, policy review, and energy forecasting. The datasets are published by NITI Aayog and can be used to study energy supply composition alongside related indicators such as consumption and sector participation.",
