{
  "generated_description": "The catalog covers statistics on money orders in India, including inward and outward flows for both number and value. It tracks Indian money orders issued and paid in India, along with foreign money orders issued and paid in India, including outward paid figures and corresponding amounts. Published by NITI Aayog, the collection supports analysis of postal money order traffic and value trends for India, useful for monitoring service performance and planning in the postal sector.",
  "generated_sector": "Information and Communications; Post"
}

{
  "generated_description": "Money Rates in India compiles key interest and policy-related rates used in the banking and credit system, including bank rate, discount rate, advance rate, lending rates, and the major commercial banks’ call money rate (Mumbai). Published by the Ministry of Statistics and Programme Implementation, it supports analysis of monetary conditions and credit costs for researchers, analysts, and policymakers. The coverage spans money rates for India, with values referenced as on 31st March.",
  "generated_sector": "Finance; Banking"
}

{
  "generated_description": "Money Stock Measures compile key indicators of India’s monetary aggregates, covering components such as notes in circulation, rupee coins in circulation, small coins, and cash on hand with banks. The series supports analysis of currency supply and cash-in-circulation dynamics, useful for researchers and policymakers studying liquidity and monetary conditions. Published by the Ministry of Statistics and Programme Implementation, the catalog provides time-consistent measures for India.",
  "generated_sector": "Finance; Economy"
}

{
  "generated_description": "The catalog covers monitoring committee information constituted at block level for rural roads under Bharat Nirman, based on a sample survey. It focuses on 2010 and provides India-wide insights into the number of blocks where vigilance/monitoring committees for rural roads were constituted, derived from survey coverage across districts, blocks, roads, habitations and beneficiary households. The data supports evaluation and oversight of rural road programme implementation and helps NITI Aayog and planners assess governance and monitoring reach.",
